<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-14206] 2.8.1 inlines POJO but ignores it since 2.9.0</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-14206</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Since 2.9.0 there is an &quot;inlineObjSupported&quot; flag in MetaInfo. It set up with false if Ignite starts up on previous versions. But actually inlining of POJO is enabled earlier.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Start AI 2.8.1 with persistence, create an index (int, pojo, int), fill with data;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Stop Ai 2.8.1, start AI 2.9.0;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Query the index.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Corrupted tree exception is raised then.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</description>
